<title>INDIA: India allocates foodgrains for domestic sales.</title>
<headline>India allocates foodgrains for domestic sales.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>India has earmarked 1.23 million tonnes of rice and 836,000 tonnes of wheat for sale at subsidised rates in the domestic market in November, the government said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>The statement said for October the government had allocated 1.31 million tonnes of rice and 867,000 tonnes of wheat to be sold through the Public Distribution System (PDS).</p>
<p>&quot;The allocation has been maintained at high levels in view of the festival season even though the offtake of rice and wheat together in the earlier months has been about 1.6 million tonnes,&quot; the statement said.</p>
</text>
